# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction and review of time-evolution {#1-introduction-and-review-of-time-evolution}"
msgstr "1. Panimula at pagbabalik-aral ng time-evolution {#1-introduction-and-review-of-time-evolution}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This notebook follows the methods and techniques of lesson 7. Our goal is to numerically solve the time-dependent Schrödinger equation. As discussed in lesson 7, Trotterization consists in the successive application of a quantum gate or gates, chosen to approximate the time evolution of a system for a time slice. We repeat that discussion here for convenience. Feel free to skip to the code cells below if you have recently reviewed lesson 7.\n"
msgstr "Sinusundan ng notebook na ito ang mga pamamaraan at teknik ng aralin 7. Ang aming layunin ay numerikong malutas ang time-dependent na ekwasyon ni Schrödinger. Gaya ng tinalakay sa aralin 7, ang Trotterization ay binubuo ng sunud-sunod na paglapat ng isang quantum gate o mga gate, na pinili upang mapalapit ang time evolution ng isang sistema para sa isang time slice. Inuulit namin ang talakayang iyon dito para sa kaginhawahan. Maaari kang lumaktaw sa mga code cell sa ibaba kung kamakailan mo lang sinuri ang aralin 7.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Following from the Schrödinger equation, the time evolution of a system initially in the state $\\vert\\psi(0)\\rangle$ takes the form:\n"
msgstr "Batay sa ekwasyon ni Schrödinger, ang time evolution ng isang sistema na nasa estado $\\vert\\psi(0)\\rangle$ sa una ay may ganitong anyo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle = e^{-i H t} \\vert \\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle = e^{-i H t} \\vert \\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $H$ is the time-independent Hamiltonian governing the system. We consider a Hamiltonian that can be written as a weighted sum of Pauli terms $H=\\sum_j a_j P_j$, with $P_j$ representing a tensor product of Pauli terms acting on $n$ qubits. In particular, these Pauli terms might commute with one another, or they might not. Given a state at time $t=0$, how do we obtain the system's state at a later time $|\\psi(t)\\rangle$ using a quantum computer? The exponential of an operator can be most easily understood through its Taylor series:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $H$ ay ang time-independent na Hamiltonian na namamahala sa sistema. Isinasaalang-alang namin ang isang Hamiltonian na maaaring isulat bilang weighted sum ng mga Pauli term na $H=\\sum_j a_j P_j$, kung saan ang $P_j$ ay kumakatawan sa tensor product ng mga Pauli term na kumikilos sa $n$ qubit. Sa partikular, ang mga Pauli term na ito ay maaaring mag-commute sa isa't isa, o maaaring hindi. Kung ang estado ay nasa $t=0$, paano natin makukuha ang estado ng sistema sa susunod na panahon na $|\\psi(t)\\rangle$ gamit ang isang quantum computer? Ang exponential ng isang operator ay pinakamadaling maunawaan sa pamamagitan ng Taylor series nito:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-iHt-\\frac{1}{2}H^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-iHt-\\frac{1}{2}H^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some very basic exponentials, like $e^{iZ}$ can be implemented easily on quantum computers using a compact set of quantum gates. Most Hamiltonians of interest will not have just a single term, but will instead have many terms. Note what happens if $H = H_1+H_2$:\n"
msgstr "Ang ilang napaka-simpleng exponential, tulad ng $e^{iZ}$, ay madaling maipatupad sa mga quantum computer gamit ang isang compact na set ng mga quantum gate. Karamihan sa mga Hamiltonian na interesado tayo ay hindi magkakaroon ng iisang term lamang, kundi maraming term. Pansinin kung ano ang mangyayari kapag ang $H = H_1+H_2$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-i(H_1+H_2)t-\\frac{1}{2}(H_1+H_2)^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-i(H_1+H_2)t-\\frac{1}{2}(H_1+H_2)^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When $H_1$ and $H_2$ commute, we have the familiar case (which is also true for numbers, and variables $a$ and $b$ below):\n"
msgstr "Kapag nag-commute ang $H_1$ at $H_2$, mayroon tayong pamilyar na kaso (na totoo rin para sa mga numero, at mga variable na $a$ at $b$ sa ibaba):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (a+b) t} = e^{-i a t}e^{-i b t}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (a+b) t} = e^{-i a t}e^{-i b t}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But when operators do not commute, terms cannot be rearranged in the Taylor series to simplify in this way. Thus, expressing complicated Hamiltonians in quantum gates is a challenge.\n"
msgstr "Ngunit kapag hindi nag-commute ang mga operator, hindi maaaring muling ayusin ang mga term sa Taylor series upang mapadali sa ganitong paraan. Kaya naman, ang pagpapahayag ng mga kumplikadong Hamiltonian sa mga quantum gate ay isang hamon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One solution is to consider very small time $t$, such that the first-order term in the Taylor expansion dominates. Under that assumption:\n"
msgstr "Isang solusyon ay ang isaalang-alang ang napakaliit na oras na $t$, upang ang first-order term sa Taylor expansion ang mangibabaw. Sa ilalim ng asumpsyong iyon:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (H_1+H_2) t} \\approx 1-i(H_1+H_2)t \\approx (1-i H_1 t)(1-i H_2 t) \\approx e^{-i H_1 t}e^{-i H_2 t}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (H_1+H_2) t} \\approx 1-i(H_1+H_2)t \\approx (1-i H_1 t)(1-i H_2 t) \\approx e^{-i H_1 t}e^{-i H_2 t}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we might need to evolve our state for a longer time. That is accomplished by using many such small steps in time. This process is called Trotterization:\n"
msgstr "Siyempre, maaaring kailanganin nating i-evolve ang ating estado para sa mas matagal na panahon. Nagagawa ito sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng maraming ganoong maliliit na hakbang sa oras. Ang prosesong ito ay tinatawag na Trotterization:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle \\approx \\left(\\prod_j e^{-i a_j P_j t/r} \\right)^r \\vert\\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle \\approx \\left(\\prod_j e^{-i a_j P_j t/r} \\right)^r \\vert\\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $t/r$ is the time slice (evolution step) that we are choosing. As a result, a gate to be applied $r$ times is created. A smaller timestep leads to a more accurate approximation. However, this also leads to deeper circuits which, in practice, leads to more error accumulation (a non-negligible concern on near-term quantum devices).\n"
msgstr "Dito ang $t/r$ ay ang time slice (evolution step) na aming pinipili. Bilang resulta, isang gate ang nililikha upang ilapat ng $r$ beses. Ang mas maliit na timestep ay nagdudulot ng mas tumpak na paglapit. Gayunpaman, nagdudulot din ito ng mas malalim na mga circuit na, sa praktikal, nagdudulot ng mas maraming pag-iipon ng error (isang hindi malalimang alalahanin sa mga near-term quantum device).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Today, we will study the time evolution of the [Ising model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ising_model) on linear lattices of $N=2$ and $N=6$ sites. These lattices consist of an array of spins $\\sigma_i$ that interact only with their nearest neighbors. These spins can have two orientations: $\\uparrow$ and $\\downarrow$, which correspond to a magnetization of $+1$ and $-1$ respectively.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, pag-aaralan natin ang time evolution ng [Ising model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ising_model) sa mga linear lattice ng $N=2$ at $N=6$ site. Ang mga lattice na ito ay binubuo ng isang hanay ng mga spin na $\\sigma_i$ na nakikipag-ugnayan lamang sa kanilang pinakamalapit na mga kapitbahay. Ang mga spin na ito ay maaaring magkaroon ng dalawang oryentasyon: $\\uparrow$ at $\\downarrow$, na naaayon sa magnetisasyon na $+1$ at $-1$ ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = - J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} - h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} X_i  \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = - J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} - h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} X_i  \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J$ describes the interaction energy, and $h$ the magnitude of an external field (in the x-direction above, but we will modify this). Let us write this expression using Pauli matrices, and considering that the external field has an angle $\\alpha$ with respect to the transversal direction,\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $J$ ay naglalarawan ng interaction energy, at ang $h$ ang lakas ng isang panlabas na field (sa direksyon ng x sa itaas, ngunit babaguhin natin ito). Isulat natin ang ekspresyong ito gamit ang mga Pauli matrix, at isinasaalang-alang na ang panlabas na field ay may anggulo na $\\alpha$ kaugnay ng transversal na direksyon,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} -h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} (\\sin\\alpha Z_i + \\cos\\alpha X_i) \\text{.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} -h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} (\\sin\\alpha Z_i + \\cos\\alpha X_i) \\text{.}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This Hamiltonian is useful in that it allows us to easily study the effects of an external field. In the computational basis, the system will be encoded as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang Hamiltoniang ito ay kapaki-pakinabang dahil nagbibigay-daan sa atin na madaling pag-aralan ang mga epekto ng isang panlabas na field. Sa computational basis, ang sistema ay ie-encode tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Quantum state            | Spin representation                        |\n"
"|:------------------------:|:------------------------------------------:|\n"
"| $\\lvert 0 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$         |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$       |\n"
"| $\\ldots$                 | $\\ldots$                                   |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 1 1 1 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Quantum state            | Representasyon ng Spin                     |\n"
"|:------------------------:|:------------------------------------------:|\n"
"| $\\lvert 0 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$         |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$       |\n"
"| $\\ldots$                 | $\\ldots$                                   |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 1 1 1 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow$ |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start investigating the time evolution of such a quantum system. More specifically, we will visualize the time-evolution of certain properties of the system like magnetization.\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayong imbestigahan ang time evolution ng ganoong quantum system. Sa partikular, ivi-visualize natin ang time-evolution ng ilang katangian ng sistema tulad ng magnetisasyon.\n"

